{# Owner decision D-245 (4 Nov 2026), P1: the global pricing rules. MD changes them; ED may look. Port of views/pricing/settings.php. #}
{% set ro = '' if canManage else ' disabled' %}
<div class="card">
  <h1>Pricing Settings</h1>
  <p class="muted">The global rules every product's price is built from (FOB, per unit, in USD). A product can override any of them on its own page. Only the MD can change these; every change is recorded in the audit log (who, when, before → after). New quotes use the new values; orders with an issued Proforma Invoice keep their prices. Never shown to clients, associates or sales staff.</p>

  <div class="alert alert-info">
    <strong>How a price is built:</strong> cost = supplier price (₹) ÷ pricing exchange rate + other costs to FOB ·
    minimum price = cost ÷ (1 − margin %) · staff floor = minimum price + team-incentive reserve ·
    associate floor = staff floor ÷ (1 − commission %) · quote price = floor × (1 + buffer %).
    Team incentive program is <strong>{{ 'on' if programOn else 'off' }}</strong>{{ '' if programOn else ' — no reserve is added to prices' }}.
  </div>

  {# D-301 / D-304: the rate in use, explained; source, date, warnings, the MD's OK for a big move, and the history. #}
  <div class="section" id="exchange-rate">
    <h2>Exchange Rate</h2>
    {% include "pricing/_fx_rate_line.njk" %}
    <p class="small muted">{{ 'Automatic' if fx.mode == 'auto' else 'Manual' }}{% if fx.source %} · source {{ fx.source }} · rate of {{ fx.date }}{% endif %}. Prices on Quotations and Proforma Invoices already issued never change.</p>
    {% if fx.waiting %}{% set w = fx.waiting %}
      <div class="alert alert-warning">
        <p><b>Waiting for the MD:</b> today's market rate ₹{{ w.market_rate | fixed4 }} ({{ w.source }}, {{ w.rate_date }}) moved {{ pricingFmt.signed(w.change_pct) }} — more than {{ pricingFmt.trim3(fxJumpPct) }}% in a day. It is not used for prices until approved.</p>
        {% if canManage %}
          <form method="post" action="/pricing/fx-rates/{{ w.id }}/decide" class="field-grid">
            <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
            <label>Reason *<input type="text" name="reason" required minlength="10" maxlength="255" placeholder="e.g. Checked with the bank — the move is real"></label>
            <div><button type="submit" name="decision" value="approve" class="btn-sm btn-success">Use this rate</button>
              <button type="submit" name="decision" value="reject" class="btn-sm btn-secondary">Keep the rate in use</button></div>
          </form>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if canManage %}
      <form method="post" action="/pricing/fx-rates/fetch" style="display:inline"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{ csrfToken }}"><button type="submit" class="btn-sm">Fetch today's rate now</button></form>
    {% endif %}
    <details><summary>History (last 30 fetches)</summary>
      <table class="list">
        <tr><th>Date</th><th class="num">Market rate (₹ per USD)</th><th>Source</th><th class="num">Change</th><th>Status</th><th>Note</th></tr>
        {% set statusLabels = { 'in_use': 'In use', 'waiting_md': 'Waiting for the MD', 'rejected': 'Not used (MD)', 'failed': 'Fetch failed — last rate kept' } %}
        {% for h in fxHistory %}
          <tr><td>{{ h.rate_date }}</td>
            <td class="num">{{ (h.market_rate | fixed4) if h.market_rate != null else '—' }}</td>
            <td>{{ h.source or '—' }}</td>
            <td class="num">{{ pricingFmt.signed(h.change_pct) if h.change_pct != null else '—' }}</td>
            <td>{{ statusLabels[h.status] or h.status }}</td>
            <td>{{ ((h.note or '') + ((' ' + (h.decided_by_name or '') + ': ' + h.decision_reason) if h.decision_reason else '')) | trim }}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
        {% if not fxHistory.length %}<tr><td colspan="6" class="muted">No rate fetched yet — the daily job fetches one every morning (see the README).</td></tr>{% endif %}
      </table>
    </details>
  </div>

  <form method="post" action="/pricing/settings">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
    <fieldset><legend>Margin and Costs</legend>
      <label class="setting-row"><span class="setting-label">{{ labels.margin_pct }} *<small class="muted">Margin on the selling price, not markup: 20% on a cost of USD 1,000 gives USD 1,250. Nobody can quote below the minimum price.</small><span class="help-line">Example: cost USD 1,000 at 20% → minimum price USD 1,250 (1,000 ÷ 0.80). Nobody can sell below it.</span></span>
        <input type="number" name="margin_pct" min="0" max="90" step="0.01" required value="{{ settings.margin_pct }}" placeholder="e.g. 20.00"{{ ro }}></label>
      <label class="setting-row"><span class="setting-label">{{ labels.other_cost_pct }} *<small class="muted">Packing, inland transport to port, CHA, inspection, documents and bank charges not already in the supplier price. A product can set its own % or USD amount.</small><span class="help-line">Example: supplier price USD 975.61 + 2.5% = cost USD 1,000.00.</span></span>
        <input type="number" name="other_cost_pct" min="0" max="100" step="0.01" required value="{{ settings.other_cost_pct }}" placeholder="e.g. 2.50"{{ ro }}></label>
      <label class="setting-row"><span class="setting-label">{{ labels.buffer_pct }} *<small class="muted">Room to negotiate: the quote price is the floor plus this %.</small><span class="help-line">Example: lowest price USD 1,287.50 + 3% → quote price USD 1,326.13; the team may agree anywhere between the two.</span></span>
        <input type="number" name="buffer_pct" min="0" max="100" step="0.01" required value="{{ settings.buffer_pct }}" placeholder="e.g. 3.00"{{ ro }}></label>
    </fieldset>

    {# D-301 (point 4, 11 Nov 2026): Automatic (fetched daily) or Manual; pricing rate = market × (1 − cushion %). #}
    <fieldset id="exchange-rate-settings"><legend>Exchange Rate (USD → INR)</legend>
      <label class="setting-row"><span class="setting-label">{{ labels.fx_mode }} *<small class="muted">Automatic: the market rate is fetched every day (Frankfurter — European Central Bank; backup open.er-api.com) and the cushion below is taken off. Manual: the rate typed below is used.</small><span class="help-line">Example: Automatic, market ₹88.40, cushion 2% → pricing rate ₹86.63.</span></span>
        <select name="fx_mode" required{{ ro }}>
          <option value="auto"{% if settings.fx_mode != 'manual' %} selected{% endif %}>Automatic — fetched every day</option>
          <option value="manual"{% if settings.fx_mode == 'manual' %} selected{% endif %}>Manual — the rate typed below</option>
        </select></label>
      <label class="setting-row"><span class="setting-label">{{ labels.fx_cushion_pct }} *<small class="muted">0 to 5 %, one decimal. Pricing rate = market rate × (1 − cushion %).</small><span class="help-line">Example: 2 → ₹88.40 × 0.98 = ₹86.63; 2.5 → ₹86.19.</span></span>
        <input type="number" name="fx_cushion_pct" min="0" max="5" step="0.1" required value="{{ settings.fx_cushion_pct or '2.0' }}" placeholder="e.g. 2.0"{{ ro }}></label>
      <label class="setting-row"><span class="setting-label">Manual exchange rate (₹ per USD) *<small class="muted">Used in Manual mode, and in Automatic mode until the first rate has been fetched. Keep it a little below the market rate as a cushion.</small><span class="help-line">Example: market rate ₹83.25 → enter ₹82.00 (about 1.5% lower); ₹80,000 ÷ 82 = USD 975.61.</span></span>
        <input type="number" name="pricing_fx_rate" min="0.0001" step="0.0001" required value="{{ settings.pricing_fx_rate }}" placeholder="e.g. 82.0000"{{ ro }}></label>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset><legend>Team Incentive Reserve</legend>
      <label class="setting-row"><span class="setting-label">{{ labels.incentive_mode }} *<small class="muted">Added to the minimum price while the team incentive program is on.</small><span class="help-line">Example: % of profit — minimum USD 1,250, cost USD 1,000, 15% of the USD 250 profit = USD 37.50 reserved for the team.</span></span>
        <select name="incentive_mode" required{{ ro }}>
          <option value="pct"{{ ' selected' if settings.incentive_mode == 'pct' }}>% of profit (minimum price − cost)</option>
          <option value="usd"{{ ' selected' if settings.incentive_mode == 'usd' }}>Fixed USD amount per unit</option>
        </select></label>
      <label class="setting-row"><span class="setting-label">{{ labels.incentive_value }} *<small class="muted">e.g. 15 (% of profit) or 1.00 (USD per unit).</small><span class="help-line">Example: 15 → staff floor USD 1,250 + USD 37.50 = USD 1,287.50.</span></span>
        <input type="number" name="incentive_value" min="0" step="0.0001" required value="{{ settings.incentive_value }}" placeholder="e.g. 15"{{ ro }}></label>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset><legend>Supplier Prices</legend>
      <label class="setting-row"><span class="setting-label">{{ labels.stale_days }} *<small class="muted">A supplier price older than this is marked "stale" on the product list; update it before quoting.</small><span class="help-line">Example: 60 → a price quoted on 1 Sep is stale from 31 Oct; "Pricing ready?" shows ✗ until it is renewed.</span></span>
        <input type="number" name="stale_days" min="1" max="3650" step="1" required value="{{ settings.stale_days }}" placeholder="e.g. 60"{{ ro }}></label>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset><legend>Order Lines</legend>
      <label class="setting-row"><span class="setting-label">{{ labels.require_product_pick }} <small class="muted">On: a goods line on a USD order must be picked from Products (so its price is checked against the floor); a goods line typed by hand is refused. Service and charge lines can still be typed. Off: goods lines may be typed by hand and are not price-checked.</small><span class="help-line">Example: on — typing "Granite slab" by hand on a USD order is refused; pick it from Products so its price is checked.</span></span>
        <select name="require_product_pick"{{ ro }}>
          <option value="1"{% if settings.require_product_pick | string == '1' %} selected{% endif %}>On — goods lines must come from Products</option>
          <option value="0"{% if settings.require_product_pick | string != '1' %} selected{% endif %}>Off — goods lines may be typed by hand</option>
        </select></label>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset><legend>Specifications and Associate Prices (D-255)</legend>
      <label class="setting-row"><span class="setting-label">{{ labels.cbm_from_mm }} *<small class="muted">From this thickness the price is per CBM, from the product's per-CBM supplier price (Market prices). A product can set its own.</small><span class="help-line">Example: 50 → 20, 30 and 40 mm are priced per m²; 50, 60, 80 mm per CBM (12.5 m² in one CBM at 80 mm).</span></span>
        <input type="number" name="cbm_from_mm" min="1" max="2000" step="1" required value="{{ settings.cbm_from_mm }}" placeholder="e.g. 50"{{ ro }}></label>
      <label class="setting-row"><span class="setting-label">{{ labels.price_request_daily_limit }} *<small class="muted">Automatic price requests an associate may make in one day; non-standard requests to our team do not count. An associate can have their own limit.</small><span class="help-line">Example: 10 → the 11th automatic "Get price" that day is refused; a non-standard request still goes to staff.</span></span>
        <input type="number" name="price_request_daily_limit" min="0" max="1000" step="1" required value="{{ settings.price_request_daily_limit }}" placeholder="e.g. 10"{{ ro }}></label>
      <label class="setting-row"><span class="setting-label">{{ labels.price_request_valid_days }} *<small class="muted">How long the price an associate gets stays valid.</small><span class="help-line">Example: 7 → a price given on 5 Nov is valid until 12 Nov; after that the associate asks again.</span></span>
        <input type="number" name="price_request_valid_days" min="1" max="365" step="1" required value="{{ settings.price_request_valid_days }}" placeholder="e.g. 7"{{ ro }}></label>
    </fieldset>

    {% if canManage %}<button type="submit">Save settings</button>{% else %}<p class="muted small">Only the MD can change these settings.</p>{% endif %}
  </form>

  <h2>Who Can Do What</h2>
  <table class="list">
    <tr><th>Permission</th><th>Default roles</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Record supplier / market prices and costs to FOB</td><td>Procurement (Executive, Manager, Director), MD</td></tr>
    <tr><td>See the full price build-up</td><td>MD, ED</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Change these settings, product overrides, commission levels and ladder, category specifications</td><td>MD only</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Change one product's specifications (hide, change, add for that product)</td><td>Roles with "Manage a product's specifications" — Admin and MD to start</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p><a class="btn-sm" href="/pricing/commission-levels">Associate commission levels and ladder</a> <a class="btn-sm" href="/products/price-rules">Price rules</a> <a class="btn-sm" href="/associates/price-requests">Associate price requests</a></p>
</div>
